# Sprint Execution File — Automated Product VFS Mapping Workflow (Refined)
# Agent: SWE | Risk: Zero Regression on Existing VFS Core
# Objective: Hardening the automated VFS mapping script and its verification suite. Address semantic trait matching failures, fix destructive GROQ query parsing errors, and establish resilient VFS Sub-Tree querying for seamless product placement into the VFS.

---

## Global Directives

- Final code output must contain ZERO comments unless strictly required for complex logical explanations.
- Follow the exact sequence defined. No scope execution begins until the previous scope is fully verified.
- The VFS invariant must hold: A product's `catalogueLocationKeys` cannot contain the ID of a `type: "header"` node.
- Sanity operations must use transactional updates to ensure atomic success/failure per product.

---

## Layer 1: Enhanced Semantic Trait Discovery Engine

### Scope Contract
Fix the brittle `.includes()` logic in the trait mapping engine. The `index.mjs` script must utilize a semantic keyword dictionary to map abstract product features (e.g., "integrated amplifier", "d/a conversion") into standard VFS leaf nodes (e.g., "Desktop Amps", "DAC/Amp Combos"). The product's `name` must also be parsed alongside its `overviewFields`.

### DoD

- [ ] 1.1 — In `scripts/product-vfs-mapper/index.mjs`: Introduce a robust `semanticMap` dictionary mapping specific VFS leaf `slug.current` strings to an array of semantic keywords. (e.g., `{'desktop-amps': ['amplifier', 'amp', 'receiver'], 'dac-amp-combos': ['dac', 'd/a converter', 'digital-to-analog']}`).
- [ ] 1.2 — Update `fetchProductTraits(productId)`: Ensure it retrieves the product `name` and all `overviewFields` safely, concatenating them into a single, normalized, lowercased "knowledge string" containing all product data.
- [ ] 1.3 — Rewrite `determineLeafNodeIds(leafNodes, knowledgeString)`: Iterate through the `leafNodes`. For each leaf node, check if its title or any of its associated semantic keywords (from `semanticMap`) strictly exist within the `knowledgeString`.
- [ ] 1.4 — Ensure the engine returns a deduplicated array of matching `_id` strings, strictly belonging `type: "link"` classification.

### Verification — Layer 1

- [ ] V1.1 — Run `node scripts/product-vfs-mapper/index.mjs --dry-run --productId="[Target_ID]"`.
- [ ] V1.2 — Validate console output against the Marantz PM6007 amplifier: It must output the exact IDs corresponding to "Desktop Amps" and "DAC/Amp Combos". Wait for success.

