## Layer 2: Atomic Update & Reset Transaction

### Scope Contract
Execute the definitive transaction that purges the product's legacy/corrupted IDs (e.g., `6vL2...`) and records the verified semantic array.

### DoD

- [ ] 2.1 — In `scripts/product-vfs-mapper/index.mjs`: Verify `resetAndPopulateCatalogueKeys(productId, determinedIds)` drops the old array strictly via integer/string mismatch replacements.
  1. Use `patch(productId)`
  2. Implement `.unset(['catalogueLocationKeys'])` followed sequentially by `.set({ catalogueLocationKeys: determinedIds })`.
  3. Commit transaction.
- [ ] 2.2 — Finalize CLI argument handling to support executing the real update using `--commit`.

### Verification — Layer 2

- [ ] V2.1 — Execute the script with `--commit` on the target product ID.
- [ ] V2.2 — Query `*[_type == "product" && _id == "[Target_ID]"][0].catalogueLocationKeys` via CLI or Vision plugin.
- [ ] V2.3 — Assert the array is rigidly populated with only the newly derived leaf-node IDs. ALL legacy IDs must be gone.

